        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=4$\n\nExtend the radius to a diameter and apply the chord product rule.",
          "worked": "Extend the radius upward to a diameter. The radius is $x+8$, so the upper diameter segment from the chord intersection is $x+16$. By the Power of a Point Theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}x(x+16)&=10\\times8\\\\x^2+16x&=80\\\\x^2+16x-80&=0\\\\(x+20)(x-4)&=0\\\\x&=4.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $x=-20$ since a length is positive.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 100,
        "responseSpace": "scaffold"
      },
