        "answer": {
          "short": "$x=3$",
          "worked": "Extend the radius upward to a diameter. The radius is $x+2$, so the upper diameter segment from the chord intersection is $2x+2$. By the Power of a Point Theorem,\n$$\\begin{align*}2(2x+2)&=4\\times4\\\\4x+4&=16\\\\4x&=12\\\\x&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
